    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 14th August 2006 the erection of a first floor extension to the roof of original ground floor addition with a width of 5.4m, a depth of 3.4m, and a height of 2.9m on the east side and 1.12m on the west side was lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the volume is below the maximum of 40 cubic metre allowance for additions to the roof, (50 cubic metres in total) for a terraced house.\r\n"
